WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:10.280
Five kinds of small birds called warblers live in the same spruce forests in summer.

2
00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:13.280
The forests are in Maine and Vermont.

3
00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:17.340
All five eat mostly insects from the trees.

4
00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:23.600
How can so many kinds of animals share one place without running out of food?

5
00:00:24.483 --> 00:00:28.103
A habitat is the place where an organism lives.

6
00:00:29.043 --> 00:00:30.783
A spruce forest is a habitat.

7
00:00:31.883 --> 00:00:35.083
A niche is the organism's role in its habitat.

8
00:00:36.163 --> 00:00:40.583
Think of the habitat as an address, and the niche as a job.

9
00:00:41.433 --> 00:00:44.133
A niche is more than one job.

10
00:00:44.813 --> 00:00:48.893
It includes what the organism eats, and where and when it feeds.

11
00:00:49.693 --> 00:00:52.933
It includes the space it uses, and what eats it.

12
00:00:53.873 --> 00:00:55.513
Take a Virginia oak forest.

13
00:00:56.113 --> 00:00:59.233
A gray squirrel and an earthworm both live there.

14
00:00:59.933 --> 00:01:02.153
The squirrel eats acorns and nuts.

15
00:01:02.833 --> 00:01:05.213
The earthworm eats dead leaves and soil.

16
00:01:06.133 --> 00:01:09.673
They share a habitat, but their niches are very different.

17
00:01:10.517 --> 00:01:16.197
A resource is something a living thing needs and takes from its habitat.

18
00:01:17.237 --> 00:01:20.857
Food, water, shelter and space are resources.

19
00:01:22.177 --> 00:01:24.837
A niche is how an organism gets them.

20
00:01:25.877 --> 00:01:29.537
When food runs short, an animal may have to search more places.

21
00:01:30.017 --> 00:01:31.677
So a niche can shift.

22
00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:35.730
A species is one kind of living thing.

23
00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:40.770
When two species need the same limited resource, they compete.

24
00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:46.030
Competition is a struggle for resources that are in short supply.

25
00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:51.890
If two species have niches that overlap a lot, they compete a lot.

26
00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:56.630
One may get most of the food, and the other may do poorly.

27
00:01:56.630 --> 00:02:00.710
If their niches are different, they compete less.

28
00:02:01.633 --> 00:02:06.253
So how can so many kinds of animals share one place?

29
00:02:07.353 --> 00:02:08.653
Different niches help.

30
00:02:09.813 --> 00:02:13.513
Species that use a habitat in different ways compete less.

31
00:02:14.433 --> 00:02:18.113
That lets more kinds of living things share one place.

32
00:02:19.093 --> 00:02:22.733
The variety of living things in a place is called biodiversity.

33
00:02:24.233 --> 00:02:27.653
Using a place differently does not remove all competition.

34
00:02:28.133 --> 00:02:28.893
But it helps.
